{
  "_comment": "BuildSparseGRM rooted on flare_lai_prod_set, so all 22 chromosomes arrive as one Array[File]. Set the method config's ROOT ENTITY TYPE to flare_lai_prod_set and confirm the member attribute name in the Terra data tab (pluralized member type); this is the repo's first set-rooted config. grm_vcfs = anc_vcf deliberately: the build script applies no marker filtering of its own beyond SAIGE's internal minMAFforGRM 0.01 and maxMissingRateforGRM 0.15, and FLARE anc VCFs are already biallelic SNVs at gnomAD-LAI panel sites. Do NOT swap in gt_vcf or ligated_vcf without adding a biallelic-SNV filter and LD pruning first - those are unfiltered conversions of the SHAPEIT4 ligated BCF and carry indels and SVs. Replace BUCKET. disk_gb 500 with the LOWDISK build script, which frees intermediates as it goes (peak ~2x total input size, not 3x+). With the original script: the build script never deletes intermediates, so peak disk is about 3x the total input size (localized VCFs + bcftools concat output + the bcftools reheader copy) plus two PLINK sets. 300 GB FAILED with 'No space left on device' during plink2 --vcf on 2026-10-10. Raise further for whole-callset inputs.",
  "BuildSparseGRM.grm_vcfs": "${this.flare_lai_prods.anc_vcf}",
  "BuildSparseGRM.analysis_samples": "gs://BUCKET/tractor_mix_pilot/analysis_samples.txt",
  "BuildSparseGRM.build_saige_grm_script": "gs://BUCKET/scripts/build_saige_plink_and_grm_lowdisk.sh",
  "BuildSparseGRM.make_plink_keep_script": "gs://BUCKET/scripts/make_plink_keep.py",
  "BuildSparseGRM.relatedness_cutoff": "${0.05}",
  "BuildSparseGRM.num_random_markers": "${2000}",
  "BuildSparseGRM.docker": "us-central1-docker.pkg.dev/broad-dsp-lrma/aou-lr/felix-pilot:0.2.0",
  "BuildSparseGRM.disk_gb": "${500}"
}
